    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1117">

                <pb facs="0938" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 612.1123/56.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The First Chief informed me this morning that the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bravo</hi> went to Tampico instead of Progreso, but that two gunboats would
                    be sent to latter place, as it the Government’s determination to keep the port
                    closed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
